          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.088,
            0.8,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "Try this with different starting numbers: (– 21), (– 6), and so on. Describe the patterns you observe."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.133,
            0.847,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "6.\t In a test, (+ 4) marks are given for every correct answer and (– 2) marks are given for every incorrect answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.177,
            0.848,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "(a)\t Anita answered all the questions in the test. She scored 40 marks even though 15 of her answers were correct. How many of her answers were incorrect? How many questions are in the test?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.259,
            0.847,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "(b)\t Anil scored (– 10) marks even though he had 5 correct answers. How many of his answers were incorrect? Did he leave any questions unanswered?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.327,
            0.847,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": "below."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.381,
            0.653,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.701,
            0.847,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "8. Imagine you’re in a place where the temperature drops by $5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ each hour. If the temperature is currently at $8 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ,$ write an expression which denotes the temperature after 4 hours."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.764,
            0.779,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "9. Find 3 consecutive numbers with a product of (a) – 6, (b) 120."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.789,
            0.847,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": "10.\t An alien society uses a peculiar currency called ‘pibs’ with just two denominations of coins — a+13 pibs coin and a – 9 pibs coin. You have several of these coins. Is it possible to purchase an item that costs + 85 pibs?"
        },
        {
